@startuml data-flow-sync
title Data Flow — Offline Sync (Happy Path)
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #2563EB
  ParticipantBorderColor #0F172A
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  NoteBackgroundColor #FEF9C3
  NoteBorderColor #CA8A04
}

participant "Renderer" as UI
participant "Local DB (sql.js)" as DB
participant "sync_outbox" as Outbox
participant "Sync Engine\n(sync-engine)" as Engine
participant "Cloud Sync API" as Cloud

UI -> DB : domain write (sale, stock adjustment, ...)
DB -> Outbox : enqueueSync() in the same db.transaction()
note over Engine : ConnectivityMonitor heartbeat\n(every intervalMs)
Engine -> Cloud : GET /health
Cloud --> Engine : 200 OK\n(transition offline -> online, or already online)
Engine -> Outbox : getPending()
Engine -> Cloud : POST /sync/push { records }
Cloud --> Engine : { accepted: [...], conflicts: [...] }
Engine -> Outbox : markSynced(accepted)
Engine -> Cloud : GET /sync/pull?entityType=X&cursor=...
Cloud --> Engine : { changes: [...], nextCursor }
Engine -> Engine : resolveConflict() per changed entity\nvs any pending local write
Engine -> DB : save nextCursor to sync_cursor

note over Outbox, Cloud
  Crash mid-sync: every outbox row has a unique idempotency_key,
  so a crash between "server accepted" and "rows marked synced"
  just re-sends already-accepted rows next pass (safe no-op).
end note

note over Engine
  Conflict rules:
  - stock_movements/audit_log/controlled_substance_log: append-only,
    never conflicts (throws if the transport ever reports one)
  - transactions/payments (financial): server wins
  - everything else: last-write-wins, merged per field (updatedAt
    or per-field fieldUpdatedAt)
end note
@enduml
